+# Task6 fix01 author completion report
+
+FIX_BASE `aa490afc2690e9517a691cc8d1ae9487a025806d`; original Task6 BASE `80c878f52c7b748efdcdb64e707d50cf410843b4`. This is the same author's first fix round. Implementation and validation are complete for scoped independent review; the author does not confer independent acceptance. Original public evidence and the original working-report prefix are preserved. All new raw evidence is beneath this directory.
+
+## Findings addressed
+
+**T6SR01 — prospective ancestry.** SAVE, MARKS and RESTORE account for the newly appended WORKING node before mutation in both S and F, and expose consistent capabilities. Existing depth/node limits apply without a new quota. `Task06FixIntegrityIT` covers the six operation/budget combinations, last accepted readable result, and atomic refusal of the next mutation. `integrity-red-01` retains the two behavioral failures; `integrity-green-01` and final covering pass.
+
+**T6SR02 — CURRENT confirmation integrity.** CURRENT checks the non-null root confirmation pointer and the selected revision's unique confirmation relation together, including null saved pointer/non-null confirmation. Mismatched, foreign and stale pointers fail instead of disappearing as null. Owner history remains distinct. The integrity test covers these branches. `current-confirmation-query-plan.json` records actual index_merge PRIMARY + transcript_confirm_once with two estimated rows; it is a plan observation, not contention evidence.
+
+**CV01 — actual HTTPS and wire boundary.** `Task06FixHttpsIT` runs the real installed application over loopback HTTPS using existing PKI, controlled secure sessions, and owner/member/outsider/admin HTTP calls, with LOCAL and S3. It checks Origin/CSRF/no-store, revision tokens 9007199254740991, 9007199254740992, 9007199254740993 and 9223372036854775806, legacy/equal dual/mismatched forms, replay, and MAX-1 mutation refusal. Cookie assertions include Secure, HttpOnly and SameSite. Actual setup and early failures are retained separately in `https-01` through `https-03`; `https-04` and final covering pass. No browser or company-login claim is made.
+
+**CV02 — complete structural provenance.** `Task06FixProvenanceIT` covers missing/extra/cross-linked parent, segment, mark, member, file, task, state, output, input and subject relationships, cycles/depth/node, session/sidecar/archive, published history and disabled route pairs on actual new-owned pipeline graphs. The extra same-input task produced a real RED in `provenance-04`. An intermediate global OR query passed that negative but failed indexed-scope qualification; its proof remains historical and unqualified. Subject narrowing was rejected because it misses cross-subject input references and charges unrelated history against maxTasks64. The final complete typed-input union uses the reviewed index prerequisite below and covers both same- and cross-subject extra tasks. Exact structural probe deletion requires zero attempt, transcript-producer and external references; restoration receipts retain the new UUIDs. Earlier04/05 did not independently capture those UUIDs and no historical receipt was fabricated.
+
+**CV03 — atomicity, phases, authority, cancellation and locks.** `Task06FixAtomicityIT` covers row/readback/audit/flush/commit failures across SAVE/MARKS/RESTORE/CONFIRM (20 fault cases), four lost-ack replay cases, exact JDBC holder, metadata admission before body transfer, and S/F epoch/lifecycle/governance/owner/identity/effective-member changes. Cancellation spans the tested phases. `Task06FixHandlesIT` exercises foreign issuer, fake/wrong-meeting, suspended REQUIRES_NEW/resumed/ended/new-holder authority. `Task06FixLocksIT` exercises 50 actual competing writes across readonly S/F, command S/F and inserted readback under default isolation and READ_COMMITTED, including body, segment FK, empty-mark FK, mark update and deletion. Direct VALUES avoids an INSERT SELECT read-lock confound. Each is included in final covering.
